  "reasoning_content": "We need answer user's request: detailed tutorial on implementing bounded LRU cache in Python using collections.OrderedDict. Include complete class, explain get and put behavior, discuss edge cases, include tests. Continue with worked example and complexity analysis. Be precise and meaningful prose and code.\n\nNeed produce final answer. Need think through content.\n\nWe need likely provide Python code. Bounded LRU cache using OrderedDict. Need complete class. Could include type hints, capacity, get, put, maybe __len__, __contains__, clear, peek? Need explain behavior: get(key) returns value or default, moves key to end (most recently used). put(key, value): if key exists update value and move to end; else if capacity full evict least recently used (first item), then insert at end. Edge cases: capacity <=0? Could raise ValueError or treat 0 as no storage. Need decide. Bounded LRU cache capacity positive. If capacity 0, put should not store? Could support capacity=0 by not storing and get returns default. But OrderedDict with maxsize 0? We can implement. Need precise. Maybe raise ValueError for negative, allow zero. Or require positive. Tutorial can choose. Let's design robust:\n\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Any, Hashable, Optional\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        if capacity < 0: raise ValueError\n        self._capacity = capacity\n        self._data: OrderedDict[Hashable, Any] = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key: Hashable, default: Any = None) -> Any:\n        if key in self._data:\n            self._data.move_to_end(key)\n            return self._data[key]\n        return default\n\n    def put(self, key: Hashable, value: Any) -> None:\n        if self._capacity == 0:\n            return\n        if key in self._data:\n            self._data[key] = value\n            self._data.move_to_end(key)\n        else:\n            if len(self._data) >= self._capacity:\n                self._data.popitem(last=False)\n            self._data[key] = value\n\n    def __len__(self): return len(self._data)\n    def __contains__(self, key): return key in self._data\n    def clear(self): self._data.clear()\n    def peek(self, key",
